\begin{align*}
AE^2 + 6AE &= 36 \\
AE^2 &= 36 - 6AE
\end{align*}

Step 2: Let $AE = x$. Thus, $x^2 = 36 - 6x$.

Step 3: Solving the quadratic equation $x^2 - 6x + 36 = 0$, we can find the two solutions for $x$: ($x_1$ and $x_2$). The foot of the altitude is at one of the two points, so we have:

